{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"Genomics England's own long-read award prices the option tranche of PromethION flow cells at less than half the per-unit price of the initial tranche, showing how hard this large public buyer negotiates on volume.","detail":"Award 039504-2024 (6 Dec 2024, Oxford Nanopore, single-operator award) is £5,234,229 for 3,900 flow cells plus consumables, about £1,342 each. The option for a further 4,400 flow cells is capped at £2,774,772, about £631 each, which is 53% lower per unit. The notice says 'associated consumables' without a split, so the per-unit comparison is approximate. This is a non-Illumina platform, so it only shows the buyer's leverage and that a national genomics programme gets steep volume tiers.","url":"https://www.find-tender.service.gov.uk/Notice/039504-2024","date":"2024-12-06","source_name":"Find a Tender (OCDS API), Genomics England notice 039504-2024","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"The known list covers only the 2025 Babies in Focus long-read awards, not the Dec 2024 ONT flow-cell award or its tiered unit prices."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"The Generation Study's short-read WGS award landed at about £656 per sample, the same figure the analyst already holds, but the tender documents add an estimated-value range showing the contract was won in a competitive 3-bid process on 30% price weighting.","detail":"The 2023 tender (036294-2023) estimated £40.5M for 30,000-65,000 genomes, equal to £623-£1,350 per genome across that range. The March 2025 award to Revvity was £29.2M for about 44,500 samples, about £656 each (29.2M/44,500), with no minimum volume. Price carried 30% of the award score and 3 bids were received. The notices name no sequencer, so the Illumina share is unknown.","url":"https://www.find-tender.service.gov.uk/Notice/036294-2023","date":"2023-12-08","source_name":"Find a Tender (OCDS API) notices 036294-2023 and 008121-2025","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"This adds the original estimate range, the 30% price weighting and the bid count to an already-known per-sample price."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"against","claim":"The largest government-backed genomics buyer is paying far more per sample for long-read data than for short-read WGS, so long-read rivals are not a near-term price threat to Illumina's volume.","detail":"Babies in Focus (060131-2025, 26 Sep 2025) awarded 1,000 ONT samples at £2,206,318 net (£2,206 each, Cambridge University Technical Services) and 1,000 PacBio samples at £1,288,000 net (£1,288 each, Eurofins UK), from 7 bids per lot. Short-read WGS in the Revvity award is about £656 per sample, so ONT is about 3.4x and PacBio about 2x that. The ONT price is also 58% above the tender's £1.4M-per-1,000 estimate, while PacBio is 8% below.","url":"https://www.find-tender.service.gov.uk/Notice/060131-2025","date":"2025-09-26","source_name":"Find a Tender (OCDS API) 060131-2025 and 047414-2025","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"F086 gives only a rough £1.3-2.2K range. This pins the lot values, the ONT premium to the tender estimate and the 7-bid competition."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"against","claim":"Genomics England's newborn programme is buying outsourced WGS capacity with no committed volume, and the cap implies about 7,000 samples per quarter, a modest run-rate of about 0.7-0.9 Pb per year.","detail":"The Revvity contract (008121-2025, signed 5 Mar 2025) covers about 44,500 samples over 21 months, up to 7,000 per quarter from Jul 2025 to Mar 2027, with no minimum. At 30x (about 100-125 Gb per genome) that is about 4.5-5.6 Pb in total, or 2.6-3.2 Pb per year, against an HT base of about 800 Gb per quarter in the known file's scale. It is a small, capped programme rather than a volume driver. The contract status field is also inconsistent: the lot shows 'cancelled' and the award 'active'.","url":"https://www.find-tender.service.gov.uk/Notice/008121-2025","date":"2025-03-05","source_name":"Find a Tender (OCDS API) notice 008121-2025","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The known file has NHS rare-disease WGS volumes but not the Generation Study's capped quarterly volume or the no-minimum term."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"Genomics England's newborn WGS contract came in 27% below its 2023 estimate of £40.5M, a sign that planned public-programme genome volume or price was scaled back.","detail":"The December 2023 notice estimated £40.5M for 30,000-65,000 genomes in the accelerated stage. The March 2025 award was £29.2M for about 44,500 samples, which is 28% below the estimate (29.2/40.5 = 0.72). It is unclear whether the cut comes from lower price per genome or lower volume, because the award sits inside the volume range. The award has a 12-month extension option that could add spend.","url":"https://www.find-tender.service.gov.uk/Notice/036294-2023","date":"2025-03-05","source_name":"Find a Tender (OCDS API) 036294-2023 vs 008121-2025","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The known file does not compare the estimate with the award for this programme."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"against","claim":"NHS and UK public labs keep buying Illumina consumables on direct awards that name the older MiSeq and NovaSeq platforms, not the NovaSeq X, so the legacy installed base is still being fed.","detail":"Northumbria University's 3-year, £300,000 award (signed 13 May 2025, 1 bid, Illumina Cambridge) covers consumables for a new MiSeq i100 Plus and 'existing NovaSeq and MiSeq instruments'. A buyer notice dated 1 Sep 2026 for the Illumina MiSeq (£156,201 net, 15 Sep 2026 to 15 Sep 2027) names no NovaSeq. A search snippet attributes that same value to the Northern Ireland HSC Business Services Organisation, so the buyer is unclear. These are small values and not clearly NovaSeq 6000.","url":"https://www.find-tender.service.gov.uk/api/1.0/ocdsRecordPackages/ocds-h6vhtk-0545b9","date":"2025-06-09","source_name":"Find a Tender (OCDS API) Northumbria T24/0068; ocds-h6vhtk-06ef73","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The known list does not include these specific awards or their platform wording."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"against","claim":"Public buyers' sole-source Illumina awards for mid-throughput consumables are small and pay list-like prices, so extra discounting is not visible in UK public data.","detail":"The NHS Grampian reagents award (042406-2025) went to SOPHiA kits and software for £376,349 on a direct award with 1 bid, and a separate NHS Grampian Illumina award is reported at £198,846 in Feb 2026. An UKRI NextSeq 2000 service plan was £45,820 net for 14 months, awarded without competition (067970-2025). A snippet lists a Contracts Finder award of £119,360 to Illumina Cambridge on 8 Jan 2026 whose goods are not described. None of these notices discloses a discount.","url":"https://www.find-tender.service.gov.uk/api/1.0/ocdsReleasePackages/067970-2025","date":"2025-10-23","source_name":"Find a Tender (OCDS API) 042406-2025, 067970-2025; bidsfactory snippet","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The known file has the F036/F077 pattern but not these NHS Grampian and UKRI awards."},
{"label":"2B","direction":"supports","claim":"Public research buyers are using open, price-weighted competition for sequencing services that can go to non-Illumina platforms, with 7 bids per lot on Babies in Focus.","detail":"Babies in Focus (GEL-RE-25161) used an open procedure, quality 70% and price 30%, and drew 7 bids and 7 final-stage bids per lot. It was split by technology (ONT vs PacBio) rather than by Illumina equivalence. This shows UK public research funders are willing to buy outsourced sequencing in competitive lots, which adds price pressure on research consumables over time, even though the work is not short-read.","url":"https://www.find-tender.service.gov.uk/Notice/047414-2025","date":"2025-08-08","source_name":"Find a Tender (OCDS API) 047414-2025 and 075853-2025","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The known list does not cover the Babies in Focus bid counts or the 70/30 award weighting."},
